# Provenance for codemirror.js
#
# codemirror.js is a frozen, minified ESM bundle of CodeMirror 6, built once
# and committed so the tutorial runs with no build step and no third-party
# module CDN. To rebuild (any machine with Node ≥ 18):
#
#   mkdir cmbuild && cd cmbuild && npm init -y
#   npm install @codemirror/state@6.5.2 @codemirror/view@6.36.4 \
#     @codemirror/commands@6.8.1 @codemirror/language@6.11.0 \
#     @codemirror/lang-python@6.1.7 @lezer/highlight@1.2.1 esbuild@0.25.5
#   cp ../cm-entry.mjs .
#   npx esbuild cm-entry.mjs --bundle --format=esm --minify \
#     --outfile=codemirror.js
#
# Built 2026-07-21 with Node v23.9.0, esbuild 0.25.5.
# All bundled packages are MIT-licensed (CodeMirror by Marijn Haverbeke and
# contributors; Lezer by the same). https://codemirror.net
